{
 "file": "sarm.mdx",
 "units": [
  {
   "id": 0,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 1924,
   "end": 1959,
   "text": "# SARM: Stage-Aware Reward Modeling",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 1961,
   "end": 2201,
   "text": "SARM (Stage-Aware Reward Modeling) is a video-based reward modeling framework for long-horizon robot manipulation tasks. This guide covers how to train SARM reward models and optionally use them with Reward-Aligned Behavior Cloning (RA-BC).",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2203,
   "end": 2319,
   "text": "**Paper**: [SARM: Stage-Aware Reward Modeling for Long Horizon Robot Manipulation](⟦0⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25358"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2483,
   "end": 2504,
   "text": "## Why Reward Models?",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2506,
   "end": 3231,
   "text": "Standard behavior cloning treats all demonstration frames equally, but real-world robot datasets are messy. They contain hesitations, corrections, and variable-quality trajectories. Reward models solve this by learning a generalizable notion of **task progress** from demonstrations: given video frames and a task description, they predict how close the robot is to completing the task (0→1). This learned \"progress signal\" can be used in multiple ways, two promising applications are: (1) **weighted imitation learning** (RA-BC), where high-progress frames receive more weight during policy training, and (2) **reinforcement learning**, where the reward model provides dense rewards for online or offline policy improvement.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3233,
   "end": 3244,
   "text": "## Overview",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3246,
   "end": 3274,
   "text": "SARM has following features:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3276,
   "end": 3395,
   "text": "1. **Stage-aware architecture**: Jointly predicts the high-level task stage and fine-grained progress within each stage",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3396,
   "end": 3502,
   "text": "2. **Subtask annotations**: Uses natural language subtask annotations to derive consistent progress labels",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3503,
   "end": 3646,
   "text": "3. **Temporal proportions**: Computes dataset-level priors (α̅\\_k) for each subtask to normalize progress across variable-length demonstrations",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3648,
   "end": 3709,
   "text": "SARM trains on a compact **stage+tau** target for each frame:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3711,
   "end": 3763,
   "text": "- **stage**: integer stage index ⟦0⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`k ∈ {0, ..., K-1}`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3764,
   "end": 3813,
   "text": "- **τ (tau)**: within-stage progress ⟦0⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`τ ∈ [0, 1]`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3814,
   "end": 3894,
   "text": "- **target encoding**: ⟦0⟧ (this is what the dataset processor produces)",
   "tokens": [
    "`y = k + τ`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3896,
   "end": 4119,
   "text": "At inference time (and in downstream RA-BC), SARM converts the raw ⟦0⟧ value into a **normalized progress** in ⟦1⟧ using dataset-level **temporal proportions** ⟦2⟧ (stored in ⟦3⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "`k + τ`",
    "`[0, 1]`",
    "`α̅_k`",
    "`meta/temporal_proportions_*.json`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4121,
   "end": 4165,
   "text": "This matches **Formula (2)** from the paper:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4210,
   "end": 4216,
   "text": "Where:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4218,
   "end": 4285,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ is within-subtask normalized time",
   "tokens": [
    "`τ_t = (t - s_k) / (e_k - s_k)`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4286,
   "end": 4355,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ is cumulative prior (sum of previous subtask proportions)",
   "tokens": [
    "`P_{k-1}`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4356,
   "end": 4405,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ is the temporal proportion for subtask k",
   "tokens": [
    "`α̅_k`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4407,
   "end": 4525,
   "text": "This ensures identical task states map to consistent progress values, even across demonstrations of different lengths.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4527,
   "end": 4576,
   "text": "## Inputs and Targets (What the new code expects)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4578,
   "end": 4670,
   "text": "SARM is trained through its processor (⟦0⟧), which:",
   "tokens": [
    "`src/lerobot/rewards/sarm/processor_sarm.py`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4672,
   "end": 4769,
   "text": "- **Encodes** images and task text with CLIP (ViT-B/32) into ⟦0⟧ and ⟦1⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`video_features`",
    "`text_features`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4770,
   "end": 4848,
   "text": "- **Pads/truncates** robot state into ⟦0⟧ (up to ⟦1⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`state_features`",
    "`max_state_dim`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4849,
   "end": 4975,
   "text": "- **Builds targets** as ⟦0⟧ (and ⟦1⟧ in ⟦2⟧/⟦3⟧) using the stage+tau encoding ⟦4⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`sparse_targets`",
    "`dense_targets`",
    "`dense_only`",
    "`dual`",
    "`y = k + τ`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4976,
   "end": 5078,
   "text": "- **Masks rewind frames** using a per-sample ⟦0⟧ tensor (rewind is a training-time augmentation)",
   "tokens": [
    "`lengths`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5080,
   "end": 5119,
   "text": "At minimum, each training sample needs:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5121,
   "end": 5156,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ (string): task description",
   "tokens": [
    "`task`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 5157,
   "end": 5231,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ images and ⟦1⟧ states from the dataset",
   "tokens": [
    "`policy.image_key`",
    "`policy.state_key`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5238,
   "end": 5257,
   "text": "## Annotation Modes",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 5259,
   "end": 5350,
   "text": "You can choose from **3 annotation modes** that determine how progress labels are computed:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5352,
   "end": 5487,
   "text": "| Mode           | Annotations Required | Heads                        | Use Case                                                     |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5624,
   "end": 5759,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | None                 | Sparse only                  | Simple tasks, quick experiments, no VLM needed               |",
   "tokens": [
    "`single_stage`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5760,
   "end": 5895,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧   | Dense (VLM)          | Dual (sparse auto-generated) | Detailed subtask tracking without defining high-level stages |",
   "tokens": [
    "`dense_only`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 5896,
   "end": 6031,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧         | Sparse + Dense (VLM) | Dual                         | Full SARM paper setup with both granularities                |",
   "tokens": [
    "`dual`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6033,
   "end": 6049,
   "text": "### Mode Details",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6115,
   "end": 6270,
   "text": "**No annotations required.** The entire episode is treated as a single stage called ⟦0⟧, and progress is linear from 0 to 1 over the episode duration.",
   "tokens": [
    "`\"task\"`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6272,
   "end": 6324,
   "text": "- **Sparse head**: 1 stage (\"task\"), linear progress",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6325,
   "end": 6351,
   "text": "- **Dense head**: Not used",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6352,
   "end": 6440,
   "text": "- **Best for**: Simple tasks, quick experiments, or when VLM annotation is not available",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6442,
   "end": 6468,
   "text": "## Set Up Your Environment",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6470,
   "end": 6543,
   "text": "1. Install LeRobot by following our [Installation Guide](⟦0⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "./installation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6544,
   "end": 6584,
   "text": "2. Install SARM dependencies by running:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6624,
   "end": 6633,
   "text": "Workflow:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6765,
   "end": 6962,
   "text": "**Only dense (fine-grained) annotations from a VLM.** The sparse head automatically uses a single ⟦0⟧ stage covering the full episode, while the dense head learns detailed subtask progression.",
   "tokens": [
    "`\"task\"`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 6964,
   "end": 7033,
   "text": "- **Sparse head**: 1 stage (\"task\"), linear progress (auto-generated)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 7034,
   "end": 7101,
   "text": "- **Dense head**: Multiple fine-grained stages from VLM annotations",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 48,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 7102,
   "end": 7200,
   "text": "- **Best for**: When you want detailed subtask tracking but don't need to define high-level stages",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7202,
   "end": 7211,
   "text": "Workflow:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 50,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7359,
   "end": 7532,
   "text": "**Both sparse and dense annotations from VLM.** Full dual-head mode as described in the SARM paper, with both high-level (sparse) and fine-grained (dense) stage predictions.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 7534,
   "end": 7591,
   "text": "- **Sparse head**: High-level stages from VLM annotations",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 7592,
   "end": 7650,
   "text": "- **Dense head**: Fine-grained stages from VLM annotations",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 7651,
   "end": 7728,
   "text": "- **Best for**: Complex multi-stage tasks where both granularities are useful",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7730,
   "end": 7739,
   "text": "Workflow:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 7891,
   "end": 7920,
   "text": "## Step 1: Subtask Annotation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 56,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7985,
   "end": 8130,
   "text": "**No annotation required!** Skip this step entirely. The model will use the episode's task description and compute linear progress automatically.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 57,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 8172,
   "end": 8276,
   "text": "Generate **dense (fine-grained) annotations only** using a VLM. The sparse stage will be auto-generated.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 58,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 8668,
   "end": 8688,
   "text": "**What gets saved:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 8690,
   "end": 8785,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ - Auto-generated sparse proportions (⟦1⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`meta/temporal_proportions_sparse.json`",
    "`{\"task\": 1.0}`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 60,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 8786,
   "end": 8855,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ - Dense temporal proportions",
   "tokens": [
    "`meta/temporal_proportions_dense.json`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 61,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 8856,
   "end": 8902,
   "text": "- Per-episode columns in ⟦0⟧:",
   "tokens": [
    "`episodes/*.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 62,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 8987,
   "end": 9072,
   "text": "  - (also time-based columns: ⟦0⟧, ⟦1⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`dense_subtask_start_times`",
    "`dense_subtask_end_times`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 63,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 9108,
   "end": 9195,
   "text": "Generate **both sparse (high-level) and dense (fine-grained) annotations** using a VLM.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 64,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 9665,
   "end": 9685,
   "text": "**What gets saved:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 65,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 9687,
   "end": 9758,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ - Sparse temporal proportions",
   "tokens": [
    "`meta/temporal_proportions_sparse.json`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 66,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 9759,
   "end": 9828,
   "text": "- ⟦0⟧ - Dense temporal proportions",
   "tokens": [
    "`meta/temporal_proportions_dense.json`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 67,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 9829,
   "end": 9875,
   "text": "- Per-episode columns in ⟦0⟧:",
   "tokens": [
    "`episodes/*.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 68,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 10047,
   "end": 10124,
   "text": "  - (also time-based columns: ⟦0⟧, ⟦1⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`*_subtask_start_times`",
    "`*_subtask_end_times`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 69,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 10152,
   "end": 10176,
   "text": "### Annotation Arguments",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 70,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10178,
   "end": 10286,
   "text": "| Argument               | Description                                                                     |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 71,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10396,
   "end": 10504,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧            | HuggingFace dataset repository ID                                               |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--repo-id`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 72,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10505,
   "end": 10613,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧    | Comma-separated list of high-level subtask names                                |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sparse-subtasks`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 73,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10614,
   "end": 10722,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Comma-separated list of fine-grained subtask names                              |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--dense-subtasks`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 74,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10723,
   "end": 10831,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧         | Generate only dense annotations (auto-creates sparse \"task\" stage)              |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--dense-only`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 75,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10832,
   "end": 10940,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧          | Camera/video key to use (e.g., ⟦1⟧)                        |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--video-key`",
    "`observation.images.top`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 76,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 10941,
   "end": 11049,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧        | Number of parallel GPU workers (default: 1)                                     |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--num-workers`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 77,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 11050,
   "end": 11158,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧           | Specific episode indices to annotate (default: all)                             |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--episodes`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 78,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 11159,
   "end": 11267,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧      | Skip episodes that already have annotations                                     |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--skip-existing`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 79,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 11268,
   "end": 11376,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧              | VLM model (default: ⟦1⟧)                           |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--model`",
    "`Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 80,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 11377,
   "end": 11485,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Number of episodes to visualize after annotation (default: 5, set to 0 to skip) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--num-visualizations`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 81,
   "kind": "quote",
   "start": 11487,
   "end": 11626,
   "text": "> **Note**: After annotation completes, 5 episodes are automatically visualized by default. Use ⟦0⟧ to skip this step.",
   "tokens": [
    "`--num-visualizations 0`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 82,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 11633,
   "end": 11662,
   "text": "## Step 2: Verify Annotations",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 83,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 11723,
   "end": 11766,
   "text": "**No verification needed!** Skip this step.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 84,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 11808,
   "end": 11864,
   "text": "Visualize annotations using the ⟦0⟧ flag:",
   "tokens": [
    "`--visualize-only`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 85,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 12174,
   "end": 12230,
   "text": "Visualize annotations using the ⟦0⟧ flag:",
   "tokens": [
    "`--visualize-only`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 86,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 12531,
   "end": 12640,
   "text": "This generates visualizations showing video frames with subtask boundaries overlaid and timeline of subtasks.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 87,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 12642,
   "end": 12669,
   "text": "### Visualization Arguments",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 88,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 12671,
   "end": 12762,
   "text": "| Argument               | Description                                                    |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 89,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 12855,
   "end": 12946,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Only visualize existing annotations (no generation)            |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--visualize-only`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 90,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 12947,
   "end": 13038,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Number of episodes to visualize (default: 5)                   |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--num-visualizations`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 91,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 13039,
   "end": 13130,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Type of annotations to visualize: ⟦1⟧, ⟦2⟧, or ⟦3⟧ |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--visualize-type`",
    "`sparse`",
    "`dense`",
    "`both`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 92,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 13132,
   "end": 13236,
   "text": "**Tip**: If annotations are inaccurate, adjust your subtask descriptions to be more specific and re-run.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 93,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 13243,
   "end": 13264,
   "text": "## Step 3: Train SARM",
