   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 116,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 17531,
   "end": 17617,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧          | SARM head to use: ⟦1⟧, ⟦2⟧, or ⟦3⟧            |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--head-mode`",
    "`sparse`",
    "`dense`",
    "`both`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 117,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 17618,
   "end": 17704,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧             | Compute every N frames, interpolate the rest (default: 1) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--stride`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 118,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 17711,
   "end": 17756,
   "text": "## Step 5 (Optional): Train Policy with RA-BC",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 119,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 17758,
   "end": 17918,
   "text": "Reward-Aligned Behavior Cloning (RA-BC) uses the trained SARM model to weight training samples based on predicted progress improvement. This requires two steps:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 120,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 17920,
   "end": 17997,
   "text": "1. **Precompute progress values** for all frames using the trained SARM model",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 121,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 17998,
   "end": 18067,
   "text": "2. **Train policy** with RA-BC weighting using the precomputed values",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 122,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 18069,
   "end": 18088,
   "text": "### How RA-BC Works",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 123,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 18090,
   "end": 18150,
   "text": "For each training sample, RA-BC computes the progress delta:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 124,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 18187,
   "end": 18403,
   "text": "Where ⟦0⟧ is the SARM progress prediction and ⟦1⟧ is the policy's ⟦2⟧. Samples with positive progress (good demonstrations) get higher weights, while samples with negative or zero progress get down-weighted.",
   "tokens": [
    "`φ`",
    "`Δ`",
    "`chunk_size`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 125,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 18405,
   "end": 18460,
   "text": "The weighting follows **Equations 8-9** from the paper:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 126,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 18462,
   "end": 18529,
   "text": "- **Soft weight**: ⟦0⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`w̃_i = clip((r_i − (μ − 2σ)) / (4σ + ε), 0, 1)`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 127,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 18530,
   "end": 18592,
   "text": "- **Final weight**: ⟦0⟧",
   "tokens": [
    "`w_i = 𝟙{r_i > κ} + 𝟙{0 ≤ r_i ≤ κ} × w̃_i`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 128,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 18594,
   "end": 18635,
   "text": "### Step 5a: Compute SARM Progress Values",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 129,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 18637,
   "end": 18720,
   "text": "First, run the SARM model on all frames in your dataset to compute progress values:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 130,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 18953,
   "end": 18965,
   "text": "This script:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 131,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 18967,
   "end": 19018,
   "text": "- Processes all frames and computes progress values",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 132,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 19019,
   "end": 19141,
   "text": "- Saves progress values to a parquet file next to the dataset on disk (defaults to ⟦0⟧)",
   "tokens": [
    "`<dataset_root>/sarm_progress.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 133,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 19142,
   "end": 19205,
   "text": "- Generates visualizations of the first N episodes (default: 5)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 134,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 19207,
   "end": 19221,
   "text": "**Arguments:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 135,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19223,
   "end": 19327,
   "text": "| Argument               | Description                                                    | Default    |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 136,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19433,
   "end": 19537,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧  | Path to trained SARM model                                     | (required) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--reward-model-path`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 137,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19538,
   "end": 19642,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧          | SARM head to use: ⟦1⟧, ⟦2⟧, or ⟦3⟧                 | ⟦4⟧   |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--head-mode`",
    "`sparse`",
    "`dense`",
    "`both`",
    "`sparse`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 138,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19643,
   "end": 19747,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧             | Device for inference                                           | ⟦1⟧     |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--device`",
    "`cuda`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 139,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19748,
   "end": 19852,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Only visualize predictions (no RA-BC computation)              | ⟦1⟧    |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--visualize-only`",
    "`false`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 140,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 19853,
   "end": 19957,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Number of episodes to visualize (default: 5, set to 0 to skip) | ⟦1⟧        |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--num-visualizations`",
    "`5`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 141,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 19959,
   "end": 20003,
   "text": "**Output format** (⟦0⟧):",
   "tokens": [
    "`sarm_progress.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 142,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20005,
   "end": 20075,
   "text": "| Column            | Description                                    |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 143,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20147,
   "end": 20217,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧           | Global frame index in dataset                  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`index`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 144,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20218,
   "end": 20288,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧   | Episode number                                 |",
   "tokens": [
    "`episode_index`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 145,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20289,
   "end": 20359,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Local frame index within episode               |",
   "tokens": [
    "`frame_index`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 146,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20360,
   "end": 20430,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Sparse head progress value [0, 1]              |",
   "tokens": [
    "`progress_sparse`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 147,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 20431,
   "end": 20501,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧  | Dense head progress value [0, 1] (if computed) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`progress_dense`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 148,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 20503,
   "end": 20539,
   "text": "### Step 5b: Train Policy with RA-BC",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 149,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 20541,
   "end": 20783,
   "text": "Once you have the progress file, train your policy with RA-BC weighting. The progress file is auto-detected from the dataset path (⟦0⟧) if not explicitly provided. Currently PI0, PI0.5 and SmolVLA are supported with RA-BC:",
   "tokens": [
    "`sarm_progress.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 150,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 21071,
   "end": 21105,
   "text": "The training script automatically:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 151,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 21107,
   "end": 21168,
   "text": "- Loads the precomputed progress values from the parquet file",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 152,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 21169,
   "end": 21232,
   "text": "- Uses the policy's ⟦0⟧ to compute progress deltas (Δ)",
   "tokens": [
    "`chunk_size`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 153,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 21233,
   "end": 21288,
   "text": "- Computes sample weights based on progress improvement",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 154,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 21289,
   "end": 21328,
   "text": "- Applies weighted loss during training",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 155,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 21330,
   "end": 21350,
   "text": "**RA-BC Arguments:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 156,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 21352,
   "end": 21473,
   "text": "| Argument                           | Description                                            | Default                 |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 157,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 21596,
   "end": 21717,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧          | Weighting strategy type (⟦1⟧ or ⟦2⟧)          | ⟦3⟧                  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sample_weighting.type`",
    "`rabc`",
    "`uniform`",
    "`rabc`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 158,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 21718,
   "end": 21839,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Path to progress parquet file                          | ⟦1⟧ |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sample_weighting.progress_path`",
    "`sarm_progress.parquet`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 159,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 21840,
   "end": 21961,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | Which SARM head's progress to use: ⟦1⟧ or ⟦2⟧ | ⟦3⟧                |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sample_weighting.head_mode`",
    "`sparse`",
    "`dense`",
    "`sparse`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 160,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 21962,
   "end": 22083,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧         | Threshold κ for high-quality samples                   | ⟦1⟧                  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sample_weighting.kappa`",
    "`0.01`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 161,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22084,
   "end": 22205,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧       | Small constant for numerical stability                 | ⟦1⟧                  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`--sample_weighting.epsilon`",
    "`1e-6`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 162,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 22207,
   "end": 22229,
   "text": "### Tuning RA-BC Kappa",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 163,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 22231,
   "end": 22394,
   "text": "The ⟦0⟧ parameter is the threshold that determines which samples get full weight (w=1). Understanding how to tune it is critical for RA-BC to work effectively.",
   "tokens": [
    "`kappa`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 164,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 22396,
   "end": 22424,
   "text": "**How the weighting works:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 165,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22426,
   "end": 22475,
   "text": "| Condition           | Weight                  |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 166,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22526,
   "end": 22575,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧     | 1.0 (hard threshold)    |",
   "tokens": [
    "`delta > kappa`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 167,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22576,
   "end": 22625,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | Soft weight from Eq. 8  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`0 ≤ delta ≤ kappa`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 168,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22626,
   "end": 22675,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧         | 0.0 (negative progress) |",
   "tokens": [
    "`delta < 0`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 169,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 22677,
   "end": 22705,
   "text": "**Diagnosing kappa issues:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 170,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 22707,
   "end": 22751,
   "text": "Monitor these WandB metrics during training:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 171,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22753,
   "end": 22830,
   "text": "| Metric                        | Healthy Range | Problem Indicator         |",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 172,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22909,
   "end": 22986,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧   | 0.3 - 0.8     | ≈ 1.0 means kappa too low |",
   "tokens": [
    "`sample_weight_mean_weight`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 173,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 22987,
   "end": 23064,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧ | > 0           | Should be positive        |",
   "tokens": [
    "`sample_weighting/delta_mean`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 174,
   "kind": "table",
   "start": 23065,
   "end": 23142,
   "text": "| ⟦0⟧  | > 0           | Variance in data quality  |",
   "tokens": [
    "`sample_weighting/delta_std`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 175,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 23144,
   "end": 23322,
   "text": "**If ⟦0⟧:** Your kappa is too low. Most samples have ⟦1⟧ and bypass the soft-weighting entirely. RA-BC becomes equivalent to vanilla BC.",
   "tokens": [
    "`sample_weight_mean_weight ≈ 1.0`",
    "`delta > kappa`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 176,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 23324,
   "end": 23361,
   "text": "**Setting kappa based on your data:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 177,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 23363,
   "end": 23559,
   "text": "The default ⟦0⟧ was tuned for the paper's T-shirt folding task (~90s episodes at 30fps). For your dataset, check the logged ⟦1⟧ and ⟦2⟧:",
   "tokens": [
    "`kappa=0.01`",
    "`sample_weighting/delta_mean`",
    "`sample_weighting/delta_std`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 178,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 23937,
   "end": 23965,
   "text": "**When RA-BC may not help:**",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 179,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 23967,
   "end": 24121,
   "text": "If your dataset is already high quality (consistent progress across all demonstrations), RA-BC won't provide much benefit since there's nothing to filter.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 180,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 24123,
   "end": 24156,
   "text": "### Multi-GPU Training with RA-BC",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 181,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 24492,
   "end": 24516,
   "text": "## Tips & Best Practices",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 182,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 24518,
   "end": 24537,
   "text": "### Choosing a Mode",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 183,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 24539,
   "end": 24617,
   "text": "- **Start with ⟦0⟧** for quick experiments - no annotation overhead",
   "tokens": [
    "`single_stage`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 184,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 24618,
   "end": 24726,
   "text": "- Use **⟦0⟧** when you want detailed progress tracking but tasks don't have clear high-level stages",
